## Assumptions &amp; Methodology

<div class="cf-assumptions reveal">
  <h3>How this forecast was built</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Revenue baseline:</strong> Monthly figures are the 7-month average from November 2025 – May 2026 (Xero P&L). No growth adjustment applied — this is a conservative flat projection.</li>
    <li><strong>Expenses baseline:</strong> Monthly cost of sales ($4,576) and operating expenses ($19,118) are the same 7-month averages. Expenses treated as stable unless a known one-off exists.</li>
    <li><strong>Overdue receivables collection:</strong> $72,844 modelled as collected over 5 months ($25k, $20k, $15k, $7.8k, $5k). This assumes active debtor management. Fiezan and Kenyon invoices are the priority.</li>
    <li><strong>Payables clearance:</strong> The $103,251 outstanding payables balance is scheduled to clear over 5 months ($30k, $25k, $20k, $15k, $13.3k), using inflows from receivables collection and operations.</li>
    <li><strong>Accrual vs cash:</strong> The P&L used is accrual-based. Cash timing may vary slightly where invoices are issued before payment is received. The forecast treats the monthly revenue figure as collected in the same month for simplicity.</li>
    <li><strong>No capital expenditure, loan repayments or tax payments</strong> beyond what appears in the operating expense lines. If any fall due in this period, cash positions will be lower than shown.</li>
    <li><strong>Data current to:</strong> 26 May 2026. Xero last refreshed 25 May 2026 22:31 AEST.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

